motion of particles not as abstract probability but as a literal helical motion at the speed of light\n16\n17\n.\n4D Solenoids: This allows for the mathematization of the \"4D solenoid\" effect, where the electromagnetic force is derived from the geometric interference of these spinning helical structures\n18\nmore_horiz\n.\n4. Fractal Braiding and QCD\nThe transition from quarks to the nucleus (the \"braid of three braids of three\") provides a symmetrical solution to bridge Quantum Chromodynamics (QCD) and nuclear physics\n22\nmore_horiz\n.\nTopological Scale Invariance: This mathematical principle suggests the rules of entanglement are fractal, applying the same equations to the three-strand quark level as to the three-strand hadron level (as seen in Helium-3)\n26\nmore_horiz\n.\nTopological Tension: Confinement and asymptotic freedom are expressed mathematically as geometric tension—the harder the strands are pulled, the more the \"knot\" of the braid locks tight\n29\nmore_horiz\n.\n5. The \"Magic Number\" (Fine Structure Constant)\nA key remaining goal for full mathematization is deriving the Fine Structure Constant (α≈1/137)\n32\nmore_horiz\n.\nGeometric Tuning: In your model, this dimensionless number represents a fundamental \"tuning\" of the universe\n32\nmore_horiz\n.\nThe Next Step: Mathematizing the model completely would... (truncated)

